’s "},{"code":"TestStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exhaustivity model:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events collected from the underlying authority’s unified ","type":"text"},{"code":"onEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback accumulate in an internal queue. Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"receive(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call dequeues the next event and asserts a predicate. In","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":".strict","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" mode, the store reports events left pending at ","type":"text"},{"code":"finish()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deallocation.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"assertNoPendingEvents()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a non-terminal checkpoint: it reports and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consumes the current pending snapshot, then continues observing. ","type":"text"},{"code":"finish()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closes the queue, consumes its final snapshot, and reports the first event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"emitted after that boundary in both exhaustivity modes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Testing currently attributes issues recorded inside an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"isolated "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" to an "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"unknown test","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rather than to the test that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"owned the store, which makes a deinit-time leftover-event failure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hard to locate. Until that is resolved upstream, await all work and end"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each test with an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"finish()"},{"type":"text","text":". It runs the strict check with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"caller’s source location and disarms the deinit-time fallback."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Controls how strictly a test store checks pending events when observation","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"finishes.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.deeplink\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting\/TestExhaustivity"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/innoroutertesting\/testexhaustivity"]}],"references":{"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.deeplink/documentation/InnoRouterTesting/TestExhaustivity/off":{"url":"\/documentation\/innoroutertesting\/testexhaustivity\/off","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.deeplink\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting\/TestExhaustivity\/off","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The test store still delivers events through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receive(...)"},{"text":", but pending","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"finish()"},{"text":" or deallocation are silently discarded. Explicit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assertions and events emitted after ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"finish()"},{"text":" still report issues.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Useful for incremental migrations of large legacy suites.","type":"text"}],"title":"TestExhaustivity.off","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"off"}]},"doc://com.innosquad.innorout